\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    R, C = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    positions = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] == 8]\n    r0, r1 = min(r for r, c in positions), max(r for r, c in positions)\n    c0, c1 = min(c for r, c in positions), max(c for r, c in positions)\n\n    # The 8s obscure a region; reconstruct it from the matching region on\n    # the opposite side of the grid.\n    h, w = r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1\n    return [[grid[R - 1 - (r0 + i)][C - 1 - (c0 + j)]\n             for j in range(w)] for i in range(h)]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[9,9,2],[9,1,3],[7,2,7],[7,7,9],[1,6,7],[6,6,7],[1,5,4],[5,1,4],[7,9,4]]}},{"step":218,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790716452.038,"t1":1790716463.678,"alias":"task-40ffb0c9","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 1 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n9 9 1 4\n4 1 7 5\n1 4 5 7\n1 9 4 3\nwhere the pair's output is\n6 9 6 6\n9 3 9 9\n3 4 9 9\n1 9 4 1\nFailed checks in this instance: 2 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"request_demos\"}.","reply":"```python\ndef transform(grid):\n    R, C = len(grid), len(grid[0])\n    cells = [(r, c) for r in range(R) for c in range(C) if grid[r][c] == 8]\n    r0, r1 = min(r for r, c in cells), max(r for r, c in cells)\n    c0, c1 = min(c for r, c in cells), max(c for r, c in cells)\n    h, w = r1 - r0 + 1, c1 - c0 + 1\n    # The covered rectangle is copied from the vertically opposite location.\n    return [[grid[R - h + i][c0 + j] for j in range(w)] for i in range(h)]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit","correct":false,"grid":[[3,1,9],[2,9,9],[2,9,9],[3,1,9],[7,2,7],[9,7,7],[7,6,1],[7,6,6],[4,5,1]]}},{"step":218,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790716463.789,"t1":1790716478.929,"alias":"task-40ffb0c9","message":"You